    "_dependencyNotes": "@solana/sysvars and @solana/zk-sdk have NO import sites in src/ but are both load-bearing — do not delete them as unused. @solana/sysvars is declared so token-2022's `@solana/sysvars ^8` peer is satisfied from this app's own resolution context; dropping it hands that to pnpm's autoInstallPeers, which is exactly how a second copy gets materialised. @solana/zk-sdk is referenced by next.config.js, which externalises the server build to `commonjs @solana/zk-sdk/node` and rewrites `@solana/zk-sdk/bundler` requests — that resolves from this package's node_modules. It is pinned EXACTLY (0.5.2, matching the root override) because a second resolved copy instantiates a second WASM module and breaks class identity with `expected instance of ElGamalKeypair`. @solana/react was removed rather than bumped to v8: it had zero import sites and its kit peer (^8.3.0) is tighter than the ^8.0.0 the rest of the tree uses. @solana/connector is deliberately held at 0.1.4; its latest (0.2.6) still hard-depends on kit ^7, so upgrading would not retire the root override that forces it onto v8 anyway.",
